(640619, 64507, 6477, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Paul!!!! a well deserved blue ribbon for you:)) and I''m impressed... two blues in a row!!!</td>', 'Congratulations Paul!!!! a well deserved blue ribbon for you:)) and I''m impressed... two blues in a row!!!', '2004-03-27 01:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(640734, 64507, 5176, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments <br/>you wait all year for a ribbon and then two come along at once<br/>I doubt that my entry for "out of place" will score high and I''m bracing myself for the comments<br/> <br/>By the way " to the stars "  post shot editing would have passed the basic rules it was converted to B/W and the contrast increased</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments you wait all year for a ribbon and then two come along at onceI doubt that my entry for "out of place" will score high and I''m bracing myself for the comments By the way " to the stars "  post shot editing would have passed the basic rules it was converted to B/W and the contrast increased', '2004-03-27 08:06:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(641288, 64362, 6576, '<td valign="top">Zmared:<br/>First I have submit my original photo and I have not been DQ''d. The only things I did in photoshop was to add some contract, size it down to 640, turn it to black &amp; white, all which is legal.<br/>Second I have used these same blinds in two other pictures, if you check my past challenges you will see them.<br/>Third I didn''t vote on this, The other members have voted on this and they must have thought it was very good for it to pull second place.<br/>Plus I am very happy to have my first ribbon.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-28 05:40:37.</i></td>', 'Zmared:First I have submit my original photo and I have not been DQ''d. The only things I did in photoshop was to add some contract, size it down to 640, turn it to black & white, all which is legal.Second I have used these same blinds in two other pictures, if you check my past challenges you will see them.Third I didn''t vote on this, The other members have voted on this and they must have thought it was very good for it to pull second place.Plus I am very happy to have my first ribbon.', '2004-03-28 06:38:57.000000', '2004-03-28 06:40:37.000000', 0),
(641749, 64507, 16301, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your second ribbon in a row. This structure/building has so much power to it, the perspective and tone really enhance that. Did you worry about the slight tilt to the right? Just curious.<br/> <br/>Good luck in your next challenges...<br/> <br/>- Thamer</td>', 'Congrats on your second ribbon in a row. This structure/building has so much power to it, the perspective and tone really enhance that. Did you worry about the slight tilt to the right? Just curious. Good luck in your next challenges... - Thamer', '2004-03-28 21:44:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(642121, 64507, 18904, '<td valign="top">I am a great fan of color. There is a total lack of blue in this photo.Of all colors there should be blue,<br/> <br/>The angle is great. Composition is OK. But there is no color.You lose points because you do not intagrate color as an aspect of your composition. While B&amp;W can be a strong format, you fail to see that there is a pervading color cast that would give a sense of motion to your picture.</td>', 'I am a great fan of color. There is a total lack of blue in this photo.Of all colors there should be blue, The angle is great. Composition is OK. But there is no color.You lose points because you do not intagrate color as an aspect of your composition. While B&W can be a strong format, you fail to see that there is a pervading color cast that would give a sense of motion to your picture.', '2004-03-29 03:43:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(642816, 64342, 17126, '<td valign="top">I''m shocked this did not win a ribbon.</td>', 'I''m shocked this did not win a ribbon.', '2004-03-29 16:32:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(642920, 64127, 6999, '<td valign="top">Haven''t been able to get on-line much recently, due to a major row with my service provider, so haven''t voted as much as I''d like. This is a very strong image though, and has been disgracefully esrved by the voters - I love the lmaost ghost-like effect of the presence of the  obttle in only the mirror world (Of course it''s obvious that it''s only out of frame - but that''s also the beauty of the trick - that it''s so simple it isn''t really a trick at all). It takes quite a developed eye to see our three-dimensional world in such a way. Great work.<br/> <br/>I don''t quite go for it enough to favourite it, not just yet. But we''ll see if it grows anymore on me.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-29 17:04:10.</i></td>', 'Haven''t been able to get on-line much recently, due to a major row with my service provider, so haven''t voted as much as I''d like. This is a very strong image though, and has been disgracefully esrved by the voters - I love the lmaost ghost-like effect of the presence of the  obttle in only the mirror world (Of course it''s obvious that it''s only out of frame - but that''s also the beauty of the trick - that it''s so simple it isn''t really a trick at all). It takes quite a developed eye to see our three-dimensional world in such a way. Great work. I don''t quite go for it enough to favourite it, not just yet. But we''ll see if it grows anymore on me.', '2004-03-29 18:03:18.000000', '2004-03-29 18:04:10.000000', 0),
(643309, 64780, 472, '<td valign="top">this is gorgeous</td>', 'this is gorgeous', '2004-03-29 22:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
